gnomato (0.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The day's count can be reset by hand from the right-click menu. The reset is
    a mark in the journal rather than a deletion, so "Today" stays a reading of
    the record and a new local day still starts it at zero. The count is also
    read when the menu opens, not only when an interval closes, so it cannot sit
    stale across midnight.
  * Only a completion sounds a cue now. Starting an interval by hand — the popup
    button or the shortcut — is silent: the cue is what announces the interval
    the completion advanced to.

 -- Yegor Chuperka <yegor-chuperka@yandex.ru>  Sat, 10 Oct 2026 13:55:52 +0200

gnomato (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Sound cues per interval kind: a pomodoro begins with an alarm and a break
    with a chime. A completion announces the cue of the interval it advances
    to, so the cue sounds even when the next interval does not start itself,
    and a start right after a completion does not repeat it. The behaviour
    switch is relabelled accordingly; the system event-sound setting keeps
    silencing the cues.

 -- Yegor Chuperka <yegor-chuperka@yandex.ru>  Fri, 09 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

gnomato (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Panel popup: a countdown ring, the interval in words, the set as a row of
    tomatoes, and start/pause, skip and reset as round buttons. The popup opens
    on a left click, the menu with the day's count and the preferences moves to
    the right click. Styles live in stylesheet.css and ship with the package.

 -- Yegor Chuperka <yegor-chuperka@yandex.ru>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 23:40:00 +0000

gnomato (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: panel countdown, configurable pomodoro and break lengths,
    set order with auto-start policies, notifications with a theme sound,
    preferences window, and an append-only journal of finished intervals.

 -- Yegor Chuperka <yegor-chuperka@yandex.ru>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
